id: scout-scope
name: Scout Scope
kind: gear
tags: tech
craftDC: Apprentice
# "You can spend 3 Actions to attempt to scan the strength of another Character."
placeCost: 3
# "Any Character that is using the Holding Back Maneuver or is aware of the scanning can make
# a Qualified Concealment Skill Check."
scanSkill: concealment
scanDifficulty: qualified
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Three Actions to read someone's Tier of Power - and their Power Level, if they are at
  their base Tier - unless they hide it with a Qualified Concealment Check.
text: >
  Scout Scope [Tech]: A handheld device capable of indicating a combatant’s individual combat
  strength.
  –Craft DC: Apprentice
  –Effects: You can spend 3 Actions to attempt to scan the strength of another Character. Any
  Character that is using the Holding Back Maneuver or is aware of the scanning can make a
  Qualified Concealment Skill Check. If they succeed, nothing happens and they automatically
  succeed on any further Concealment Skill Checks to avoid being spotted by a Scout Scope for
  the remainder of the Combat Encounter. If their number of Holding Back stacks would
  decrease below their current number, they lose this benefit. If they fail, you become
  aware of their current Tier of Power. If their current Tier of Power is the same as their
  base Tier of Power, you also learn of their Power Level.

  While you hold this Basic Item, you have access to the Scan Adventuring Maneuver.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Scan: 3 Actions at the one character targeted, and a card. The Concealment Check is rolled
# from their own sheet at Qualified - the way the Treatment Maneuver's Medicine Check is - and
# the card has the two answers, for whoever plays them: Hidden, the Check was met; Read, it
# was not, or they could not make one.
#
# Read tells the scanner alone, in a whisper, their current Tier of Power - and their Power
# Level too when that Tier is their base Tier.
#
# Hidden is remembered on them for the rest of the Combat Encounter, with the Holding Back
# stacks they had: every later scan by a Scout Scope finds them hidden without a Check, until
# those stacks drop below that number. It is kept with the other once-per-Encounter uses and
# cleared when an Encounter begins or ends.
#
# --- What the table keeps ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Whether they are aware of the scan, which is what decides whether they may make the Check
# without Holding Back. The card offers the Check to whoever plays them either way.
#
# --- What is not built ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "While you hold this Basic Item, you have access to the Scan Adventuring Maneuver." The
# Adventuring Maneuvers are not in this system yet.
